     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{3}\">\\frac{2}{3}</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample Space:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Letter side</td>\n<td>Red 1</td>\n<td>Red 1</td>\n<td>Orange 1</td>\n<td>Orange 2</td>\n<td>Purple 3</td>\n<td>Orange 4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Number side</td>\n<td>Blue A</td>\n<td>Green A</td>\n<td>Green B</td>\n<td>Red C</td>\n<td>Brown D</td>\n<td>Blue E</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Even: Orange 2, Orange 4, which makes 2 outcomes.</p>\n<p>Green: Green A, Green B, which makes 2 outcomes.</p>\n<p>They are mutually exclusive.</p>\n<p>You can use the Addition Rule for Mutually Exclusive Events:</p>\n<p>If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are mutually exclusive events, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{or}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ P}}\\left( F \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(even or green) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
